body: |-
  ## Architecture

  The ambient system has three layers:

  **Layer 1: Observation** — Events flow from hooks (post-write, stop) and MCP tool dispatch (9 emission points) into `.paradigm/events/stream.jsonl`. Append-only, bounded at 1000 events, queryable by type/source/symbol/agent/time.

  **Layer 2: Processing** — The nomination engine scores each event against all agent attention patterns (4 dimensions: symbol, path, concept, signal). Agents above their threshold generate nominations. Overlapping nominations form debates. Data policy is enforced before scoring (agents can't observe denied paths).

  **Layer 3: Surfacing** — Nominations surface via MCP tools (`paradigm_ambient_nominations`), recovery preamble (critical/high auto-surface at session start), and Platform UI (real-time SSE stream + nomination panel with accept/dismiss).

  ## The Learning Loop

  ```
  DO → RECORD → OBSERVE → NOMINATE → ENGAGE → LEARN → ADAPT → DO
  ```

  - adjustAttentionFromFeedback: >60% dismissed → raise threshold, >80% accepted → lower
  - autoPromoteJournalEntries: pattern_discovered + confidence >= 0.8 → notebook
  - Notebooks feed into buildProfileEnrichment for next session

  ## Data Sovereignty

  Four trust rings enforced at every boundary:
  1. project-locked (events, work-log, decisions)
  2. user-scoped (journal entries)
  3. creator-upstream (anonymized metrics only)
  4. network-public (aggregated stats, opt-in)

  ## Deliverables

  | Version | Focus | Files |
  |---------|-------|-------|
  | v5.1.0 | Core runtime — engine, MCP tools, data policy, hooks, IDE adapters, university | 51 |
  | v5.2.0 | Platform UI, learning loop, cross-session surfacing, substantive briefs | 17 |
  | v5.3.0 | Symphony relay, graduation candidates, journal promotion, surfacing config, SSE, expanded emission | 14 |

  ## Next Steps

  - Run paradigm shift in deus-backend and deus-frontend to activate ambient
  - Create .agent files for the workspace agents
  - Live test the full pipeline: edit → event → score → nomination → engage → learn
  - Verify Platform UI renders events and nominations correctly
